//
// PROBE: use and use. (Bund/src/stdlib/functions/bund/bund_use.rs:9-59).
//
// use fetches its operand as a URL and evaluates the text in this VM (:31-33),
// so a word the library registers stays registered. A bare path is not a URL
// to curl, so a library is named file:///absolute/path; building it from cwd
// is how the reference's own examples name their data files. The capture runs
// from the repository root.
//
"probe: use loads a library by file:// URL and keeps what it registers" println
cwd "file://{A}/tests/probes/data/uselib.bund" format use
"lib.answer" bund.eval println
"probe: use. takes the URL from the workbench" println
cwd "file://{A}/tests/probes/data/uselib.bund" format . use.
"lib.answer" bund.eval println
